          "lineage": "Pleurobranchus",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "Body ovate and large; body length 92 mm, width 78 mm in living animal; ground color light brown. Mantle widely spreads to covered whole foot; mantle edge slightly undulated. Dorsal markings milky white double rings around tubercles decrease in size toward to mantle edge. Translucent white lines on dorsal surface, short, irregular length. Dorsal tubercles small and rounded; increase in number to edge of mantle. Rhinophores short and enrolled; upper half dark brown; joined basally. Oral veil reversely trapezoid; deeper in color to posteriorly. Gills on right side between mantle and foot; gills bipinnated with 25 pinnae alternated on each side; central axis dark. Foot wide; anterior unilabiate; metapodium short and blunted.",
